## What a `type: meta-type` instance is

**A meta-type is the substrate / access-protocol classification of a type** — a memorial of `type: type` whose role is naming a distinct way that instances of types-using-this-meta-type are stored and accessed.

Instances of a meta-type are themselves type memorials.  Each type memorial carries a `has-meta-type:` typed-edge declaring which meta-type's instance-protocol it follows.

Direct lift of the Common Lisp MOP **metaclass** concept, named `meta-type` to align with the corpus's existing type vocabulary rather than `class`.

Meta-Type is **abstract** — direct instances are not authored.  Concrete subtypes (`markdown-meta-type`, `code-meta-type`, future database-meta-type) define the actual substrate protocols.

Meta-Type is a subtype of [`meta`](meta.md) — memorials about the memory system itself.

## The two-axis classification

The corpus classifies memorials along two orthogonal axes:

| Axis | Question it answers | Example values |
|---|---|---|
| `type:` | What KIND of content does this memorial hold? | `decision`, `plan`, `library`, `predicate`, `bug` |
| `has-meta-type:` (via the type) | How is this memorial stored / accessed? | `markdown-meta-type` (default), `code-meta-type`, future `database-meta-type` |

A memorial's full classification: `(type: library, has-meta-type: markdown-meta-type)` (today, implicit) or future `(type: namespace, has-meta-type: code-meta-type)`.

## Concrete meta-types

- **[`markdown-meta-type`](markdown-meta-type.md)** — the default; instances are markdown files with YAML frontmatter, accessed via standard search / show / tree tooling
- **[`code-meta-type`](code-meta-type.md)** — source-code repositories; instances are reified at single granularity (one repo) with detail in a per-repo xref index

