## When `extends: meta-type` helps

Author a new concrete meta-type memorial when introducing a new substrate / access protocol that future types will use.  Each concrete meta-type:

- Documents the substrate (where instances live)
- Documents the access surface (which tools / queries operate on instances)
- Documents the discoverability protocol (how an agent finds instances of types using this meta-type)
- Names any opt-in flags consumers use to include this meta-type in queries

## Not instantiated directly

Don't write a memorial with `type: meta-type` — write one of the concrete subtypes.  The `abstract?: true` schema flag marks this class as non-instantiable.

